# .dockerignore for ROOT-CONTEXT builds.
#
# Services that build from the repo root:
#   az acr build ... -f ./src/<svc>/Dockerfile .
# That is the six .NET services plus banker-copilot-service (Python), which
# builds from the root because it COPYs shared config/ manifests. Everything
# else builds from its own directory and has its own .dockerignore.
#
# Keep this list in step with docker-compose.yml: any service declaring
# `context: .` must appear below, or its build fails on a missing COPY path.
#
# IMPORTANT — do not add trailing slashes to rules. `az acr build` compiles each
# rule to an anchored regex (azure/cli/command_modules/acr/_archive_utils.py,
# class IgnoreRule) and only strips trailing slashes for `!` negations. A rule
# written as `infra/` becomes `^infra/$`, but directory entries are named
# `infra` with no trailing slash, so the rule silently never matches. The old
# version of this file used trailing slashes throughout, which is why the upload
# was 323 MiB (113 MiB compressed) instead of ~1 MiB.
#
# This is an allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include exactly what the
# root-context Dockerfiles COPY. If a Dockerfile starts needing another root
# file, add a matching `!` rule here or the build will fail on a missing path.

# Ignore everything at the top level.
*

# Re-include only what the root-context Dockerfiles COPY. Parent directories do
# not need their own `!` rule: az acr build always walks into ignored
# directories, so a deeper exception still applies.
!Directory.Packages.props
!src/shared/Contracts
!src/shared/Observability
!src/shared/Auth
!src/account-service
!src/prompt-eval-service
!src/transaction-service
!src/transfer-service
!src/user-service
!src/authority-service
!src/banker-copilot-service

# Config files COPYed by name in the runtime stages. These are individual files,
# not directories: `config` itself stays ignored so an unrelated file dropped in
# there never silently enters the build context.
!config/authority-policy.yaml
!config/copilot-tools.yaml
!config/harness-limits.yaml
# Embedded as a resource by src/shared/Auth (LogicalName
# Banking.Auth.jwt-audiences.yaml), so every .NET image needs it at compile
# time even though no Dockerfile COPYs it by name.
!config/jwt-audiences.yaml

# Re-exclude build output inside the re-included trees. These rules come last,
# so they take priority over the `!` rules above.
**/bin
**/obj
**/obj2
**/obj.old
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.pyc
# mutmut copies the service into this sandbox to mutate it; it is a test
# artifact and must never reach an image.
**/mutants
**/.vs
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
